  "reasoning": "For federal races in Wisconsin in 2026, there is no U.S. Senate race on the ballot; the key federal contests are the eight U.S. House seats plus the presidential race in a core swing state.[14][7] The most recent Marquette Law School Poll generic congressional ballot for Wisconsin shows Democrats leading Republicans by 47% to 45% among registered voters, a 2\u2011point Democratic edge, and by 8 points among likely voters, indicating a slight but real Democratic advantage in current federal preferences.[16] At the same time, statewide coverage and forecaster assessments describe Wisconsin as a \"competitive\" and \"core swing state\" rather than clearly aligning with either party structurally, and Trump\u2019s job approval sits at 40% approve, 58% disapprove, underscoring volatility rather than a stable partisan tilt.[7][15] Cook\u2019s statewide Partisan Voting Index classifies Wisconsin as EVEN (no net advantage for either party), so combining an EVEN structural baseline with a narrow D lead in current polling supports rating the state as a genuine Toss\u2011up with a modest Democratic edge right now.",
